{"name":"Armada","hex":"#536762","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Armada","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The Spanish Armada which sailed against England in 1588.","A village in Michigan."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Armada"}],"entries":[{"title":"Portuguese India Armadas","blocks":[{"text":"The Portuguese Indian Armadas were the fleets of ships funded by the Crown of Portugal, and dispatched on an annual basis from Portugal to India. The principal destination was Goa, and previously Cochin. These armadas undertook the Carreira da Índia from Portugal, following the maritime discovery of the Cape Route, to the Indian subcontinent by Vasco da Gama in 1497–99."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Portuguese_Carracks_off_a_Rocky_Coast.jpg/330px-Portuguese_Carracks_off_a_Rocky_Coast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portuguese_India_Armadas"},{"title":"2nd Portuguese India Armada (Cabral, 1500)","blocks":[{"text":"The Second Portuguese India Armada was assembled in 1500 on the order of King Manuel I of Portugal and placed under the command of Pedro Álvares Cabral. Cabral's armada famously discovered Brazil for the Portuguese crown along the way. By and large, the Second Armada's diplomatic mission to India failed, and provoked the opening of hostilities between the Kingdom of Portugal and the feudal city-state of Calicut. Nonetheless, it managed to establish a factory in the nearby Kingdom of Cochin, the first Portuguese factory in Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Cabral_voyage_1500.svg/330px-Cabral_voyage_1500.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2nd_Portuguese_India_Armada_(Cabral%2C_1500)"},{"title":"Armada (gamer)","blocks":[{"text":"Adam Lindgren, better known as Armada, is a Swedish former professional Super Smash Bros. player. He is widely considered one of the greatest Super Smash Bros. Melee players of all time and the greatest Melee Peach player of all time. Lindgren has won several major tournaments: he is a three-time champion of GENESIS, two-time champion of EVO, two-time champion of Apex and one-time champion of The Big House. Considered one of the historical \"Five Gods\" of Melee, alongside Jason \"Mew2King\" Zimmerman, Joseph \"Mang0\" Marquez, Juan \"Hungrybox\" DeBiedma, and Kevin \"PPMD\" Nanney, Lindgren was ranked one of the top two Melee players in the world every year from the beginning of formal rankings in 2013 until his retirement from singles tournaments in 2018, with Lindgren ranked as the number one Melee player in the world in 2015 and 2016. \nA 2021 list compiled by PGstats ranked Lindgren as the second-greatest Melee player of all time."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Heir_5_-_Armada_%28portrait_crop%29.jpg/330px-Heir_5_-_Armada_%28portrait_crop%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armada_(gamer)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Goa-Vasco_03-2016_02_Vaddem.jpg/500px-Goa-Vasco_03-2016_02_Vaddem.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Goa-Vasco_03-2016_02_Vaddem.jpg/1280px-Goa-Vasco_03-2016_02_Vaddem.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Goa-Vasco_03-2016_02_Vaddem.jpg/500px-Goa-Vasco_03-2016_02_Vaddem.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A brief view of the Indian city of Vasco da Gama","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGoa-Vasco_03-2016_02_Vaddem.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com